  "id": "alabaos_gualies_pacifico",
  "name": "Alabaos and gualíes (Colombian Pacific wake songs)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Alabaos are the unaccompanied sacred songs that cantadoras and cantadores of Colombia's Pacific coast sing at wakes and novenas for adults, a leader raising verses that the gathering answers; gualíes, also called chigualos, are the songs and rounds of the wake for a dead child, sung with bombo, cununo and guasá. Both are documented by Colombia's Ministry of Culture among the Afro-Pacific traditions of Chocó, Cauca and Nariño. The membrane-drum card stands in for the bombo, the hand-drum card for the cununo and the shaker card for the guasá.",
  "recipe": "classic modern alabaos and gualíes, funeral Lament, African diasporic branch, Afro-diasporic ritual devotional fulía. single leader group response, live take. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, hand drum source shaker source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
